export anchor ChalkboardStyle:
    number: 239
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Chalkboard
    idea:
        The whole dashboard is written up on a slate chalkboard in a wooden
        frame, with handwritten headings, wobbly chalk boxes, tally marks
        beside the counts, hatched chalk bars and soft eraser smudges.
    base: dark
    palette:
        slate: #27302c, the board, the page and the style sheet
        deepSlate: #202824, the header strip and field fills
        smudge: #323b37, the lightest eraser smudge, the peak any text sits on
        frame: #5a3d26, the wooden frame and the chalk tray
        chalk: #ecebe4, text, box outlines and last week bars
        dust: #b9bdb5, meta, labels and dates
        yellow: #f2e18c, the primary button, this week bars, progress hatching, the Home circle and focus
        blue: #a8d4f0, links and the activity arrows
        ok: #b9e4a7, On track text and check circle
        risk: #f7c38a, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #f4a9b8, Behind and overdue text, crossed square, clock and the overdue tally
    type:
        Two stacks. Headings and counts are handwriting, Chalkboard SE,
        Chalkboard, Segoe Print, Bradley Hand, Comic Sans MS, cursive, with
        the greeting 42px at 700, counts 40px, section headings 28px and box
        titles 20px. Body text is Trebuchet MS, Segoe UI, sans-serif at 16px
        and 1.55, meta 14px italic in dust. All chalk text carries a faint 1px
        chalk blur.
    layout:
        The screen is a chalkboard inside a 14px wooden frame with a chalk
        tray along the bottom edge holding three drawn chalk sticks. Across
        the top the Brightwork name is written by hand, the six nav words
        follow with a wobbly yellow circle drawn round Home, then a dashed
        chalk search box, a chalk bell, a yellow outlined New project box and
        Mara Okafor. The greeting Good morning, Mara! is written large with a
        squiggle under it, then the date and a pink line reading 4 tasks are
        overdue with a clock. Four wobbly chalk boxes hold the counts, with
        tally marks drawn beside active projects and overdue tasks. Projects
        is a three column grid of wobbly boxes, each with the handwritten
        name, category, a status mark drawn in chalk with its word, a hatched
        yellow progress bar with the percent, tasks done and due date. Below,
        the chart is chalk columns across all fourteen days, last week as
        plain chalk outlines and this week hatched yellow, with values on top
        and a written note of the totals, beside the activity written as a
        list with blue chalk arrows. Soft eraser smudges sit behind the
        content. Below 900px the projects go to two columns and the chart and
        list stack, below 600px everything is one column and the frame thins
        to 6px.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px box padding, 24px gaps, 40px between board sections.
    density: Medium. Boxes are generous like a teacher's board.
    corners: Hand drawn. Every box uses uneven elliptical corners so no two edges match.
    borders:
        2px chalk lines with uneven corners, dashed for the search box, a 14px
        wooden frame round the board.
    shadows:
        No drop shadows. Text carries a 1px chalk blur and the board carries
        soft white smudges at 4 to 6 percent.
    icons:
        Chalk line icons at 2.2px stroke with rough round ends. Status uses a
        drawn circle with a tick, a triangle with a bang and a crossed box,
        always with the word, overdue a clock.
    focus: A 3px dashed yellow outline offset 4px, like a ring drawn in chalk.
    tone: Friendly classroom, such as Good morning, Mara!, Still to do and What happened today.
